        "answer": {
          "short": "$S=180(n-2)^\\circ$.\n\nAn $n$-sided polygon divides into $n-2$ triangles.",
          "worked": "The polygons with $5$, $8$ and $12$ sides divide into $3$, $6$ and $10$ triangles respectively. In each case there are two fewer triangles than sides.\n\nAn $n$-sided polygon divides into $n-2$ triangles. Each triangle has angle sum $180^\\circ$, so\n\n$S=(n-2)\\times180^\\circ$.",
